/**
 * @page common_parameters Common public API parameters
 * 
 * @section Device_index Module index
 * 
 * Some of the SDR device configuration functions from the @ref api "public API" accept a parameter called <b>moduleIndex</b>, which addresses a specific module on a SDR device.
 * Index of a module is used to specify the target module whose configuration will be updated or retrieved. A typical example of a module is LMS7002M RF chip, which is present on all LimeSDR boards. 
 * Parameter <b>moduleIndex</b> should always be set to value <b>0</b> for LimeSDR boards that only have a single RF chip. Otherwise, if SDR device or a integrated system has multiple 
 * RF chips or other modules, this parameter must be set to the appropriate index to target the correct module.
 *
 * Module indexes always start with value <b>0</b>. The last module on a system or device is indexed as <b>total module count - 1</b>.
 * 
 * @section device_ch_indexes Channel indexes
 * 
 * Channel indexes always start from <b>0</b> and the last channel index is <b>total channel count - 1</b>.
 * 
 * Channel indexes are associated with appropriate SDR device modules. SDR devices with different modules can support a different count of channels. Moreover, the actual device channel count also depends on 
 * the number of physical traces that interconnect the module with the actual Tx/Rx ports.
 * 
 * A single LMS7002M module supports two channels at a time (Channel A and channel B). Therefore, SDR devices that use a single LMS7002M module can have a total of two channels. SDR devices with multiple LMS7002M
 * modules can have more physical channels. However, a single LMS7002M module on a multi module SDR device is able to manage only two channels at a time. Therefore, channel indexing also relies on correct 
 * @ref Device_index "module indexing". LMS7002M module channel A index is <b>0</b> and channel B index is <b>1</b>. The following channel indexes can be defined as a simple const variables: `const uint8_t ChA = 0;` 
 * and `const uint8_t ChB = 1;`.
 * 
 */
